ord-257rig-i4a"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-i4a"],"id":"long.record-257rig-i4a","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.110 (Bounds for intervals with zero divisor counts)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.110, p. 75, label record:257rig-i4a","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that $X_A(2)=p/(2^cv)$ for an infinite positive support $A$ and an odd positive integer $v$. For every $\\varepsilon>0$ there is $B$ such that, for $N\\ge1$, a run of $h$ zero divisor counts starting after $c+N$ satisfies $h\\le\\varepsilon\\log_2N+B$. In fact this conclusion holds without rationality: fix any $a\\in A$. Every $a$ consecutive positive integers include a multiple of $a$, where $c_A$ is positive. Hence $h\\le a-1$, so one can take $B=a-1$. The zero-run conclusion therefore imposes no additional restriction on a fixed nonempty support, regardless of the tail estimates used in the linked proof.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i4a","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i4a","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i4a%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_zero_run_le_eps_logb%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i4a%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_zero_run_le_eps_logb%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_zero_run_le_eps_logb"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b2